               1 2                 3
0000000000000000 t cpu_startup_entry
1: the kernel virtual address of the symbol
    * if staring with ffffffffc0 means loadable kernel modules
2: type
    * T: global text (code) symbol
    * t: local (static) symbol
    * D: global initialized data
    * d: local initialized data
    * B: global uninitialized data
    * b: local uninitialized data (BSS)
    * R: read-only data
    * r: local read-only data
    * W: Weak symbol
    * A: Absolute symbol
    * N: Debugging symbol
3: symbol name
    * if starting with __, usually means a helper function
    * inlined symbol will not apprear
    * perf_trace_xxxxxx
    	* not a real driver function, it is kernel auto generated symbol used by perf/ftrace. Called after a tracepoint fires. Don't kprobe this.
    * trace_event_raw_event_xxxx
    	* internal ftrace glue code, don't kprobe this
    * trace_raw_output_xxxx
        * Another ftrace formatting helper, don't kprobe this
    * __bpf_trace_xxxx
        * for eBPF programs to attach to, don't kprobe it.
	* eg. `tracepoint:amdgpu:amdgpu_bo_create`
    * __bpf_trace_tp_map_xxxx
        * Map helper for tracepoints, don't probe it
    * event_xxxx
        * ftrace event descripter. Metadata, not executable code
